<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birendra of Nepal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945–2001</span> · Also known as King Birendra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birendra (1945–2001) was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> from 1972 to 2001. He ruled at first through the partyless panchayat system, but the People's Movement of 1990 forced him to legalise political parties and accept a constitution making him a constitutional monarch. He was killed with his queen, Aishwarya, and other members of the royal family in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narayanhiti-palace">Narayanhiti Palace</a> massacre of 1 June 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birendra-of-nepal.jpg" alt="Birendra of Nepal" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CAPTAIN MEDUSA · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birendra_Bir_Bikram_Shah_c._1967_(restoration).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
